# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# local learner data: the SQLite file and the synthesised audio cache, which
# lives at data/audio. The audio is a cache - deleting it is safe but costs real
# money to rebuild, so keep backups. Kept out of public/ deliberately: a
# standalone build replaces that directory, which would orphan the cache.
/data

# generated by `npm run wordlist`, ~500KB each, rebuildable for free from public
# lists. Deliberately narrower than /src/data: samples.json is generated by an
# LLM and costs money to rebuild, so it is committed.
#
# placement.json is committed too, and used not to be. It is 3KB, not 500KB, and
# leaving it out meant a deploy could ship the code that reads it without the
# data it reads - which is exactly what happened when the Chinese test moved to
# HSK: production kept serving the old subtitle bands from whatever had last
# been generated on the box, and the deploy went green. It also carries the
# provenance line NOTICE.md points at, so a repo without it claims attribution
# for data it does not contain.
/src/data/*/frequency.json
/src/data/*/anchors.json

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Stray curl cookie jars: a mistyped "curl -b " writes a file literally
# named -b, and git add -A has swept one into a commit before.
-b
